WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:06.220
I have genuinely good news for you from the
a world of vaccines in Washington state.

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:10.510
This is a loss for the Anti Vaccine Movement,
which is a win for society.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:15.360
Uh, and children who can't be vaccinated,
parents will no longer be allowed to get their

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:21.500
kids vaccine exemptions in Washington state
for so called personal or philosophical reasons.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:27.250
This is for the MMR vaccine if their kids
are going to go to daycare or to school.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:32.560
Now this is good, but it's also a relatively
small win and I'll explain that in a second.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:39.520
Um, as you may know, Washington has some anti
vaccs elements and that has led to a spike

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.040
in measles cases.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.620
And the governor, Jay Inslee, who is also
running for president says no more personal

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.190
or philosophical exemptions.

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.670
Now that's good.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:55.330
The problem is most of the exemptions that
people are getting in Washington are religious,

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:56.570
religious exemptions.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:57.960
Those are still available.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.100
Of course medical exemptions are in place
as well.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:04.650
And those are the the only ones that we actually
need a, there may be medical reasons why someone

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:09.720
should not be vaccinated, but as, as long
as we don't do away with the religious exemptions,

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:16.281
um, this is going to remain a major problem
and, uh, it's great that right now, uh, you

00:01:16.281 --> 00:01:21.330
will no longer be able to say I'm personally
opposed to vaccines.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:28.760
I have philosophical objections to vaccination,
but the overwhelming majority of the non medical

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:31.000
exemptions in Washington are religious.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:36.410
So when you get rid of personal and philosophical,
it's very easy to say, well, what I mean is

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:39.650
it's my religion who can tell you that it's
not right.

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:46.770
Uh, and more importantly, something like 95
or 96, maybe even 98% of the non medical exemptions

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.320
are religious to begin with.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.440
So we've got to deal with this.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:55.690
We should praise the fact that Washington
state is doing the right thing here, but you're

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:59.830
not actually going to deal with this for as
long as someone can say, my religion tells

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:05.659
me that, uh, uh, I should not, uh, get, get
my kid vaccinated.

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:09.009
And of course, philosophical exemptions are
pretty ridiculous.

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:15.010
If you're an anti tax activists and you say,
I'm philosophically against taxation, uh,

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.100
it's called the sovereign citizen movement.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.100
It doesn't work.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.780
The government says that that's not a good
explanation.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:26.690
If you say you're philosophically exempt from
stop signs, stop signs are necessary and good

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:30.240
for society, I don't think you're allowed
to get away with that.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:32.400
This needs to be considered the same way.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.160
It's the right decision that Washington is
making, but we've got to get rid of those

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.050
religious exemptions.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:41.750
Germs don't care about your philosophy.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.510
They also don't care about your religion.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:48.640
They'll infect you or your kid or the other
person's kid who's immunocompromised, whether

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:55.080
or not you are religious or whether you have
a philosophical disagreement with vaccination.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:03:00.190
And I get really bummed out when I do a story
like this because every time I get emails

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:06.130
from people who say they love the show, but
I'm totally wrong on vaccines and I should

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:12.220
look at Andrew Wakefields work, who of course,
uh, lost his medical license for his deception

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:18.800
on this issue or the medical authorities say
vaccines aren't safe or autism, all of this

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:19.800
stuff.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:25.700
Um, it, it, it's truly and deeply depressing
to me that even people in our audience who

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:31.709
are mostly informed about what's going on
have fallen hook, line and sinker for the

00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:33.470
Anti Vaccine Movement.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:35.910
Depressing, but a small win, if nothing else
in Washington state

